//
// ⚠ MEASURED UNMOVED BY THE 2026-09-17l LANDING, on its own armed binary: REFUSED on base and
// REFUSED armed, byte-identical sentence. It is NOT closed by that change and not by a strict
// extension of it — reason 3, the arm that would close it is a DIFFERENT change with its own
// unpriced cost, and here is why precisely:
//   the landed change addresses the PLACE, because `match s.arr { [_, ref mut y] => *y = 99 }`
//   must write THROUGH to s.arr (spec pat.refbind.binds-place-reference; rustc src=99).
//   `for x in s.arr` is the OPPOSITE: an array is IntoIterator BY VALUE, so the loop iterates a
//   COPY and a write to s.arr inside the body must NOT be visible to the remaining iterations.
//   Addressing the place here would be a miscompile in the other direction. The repair is a
